{"TV":{"id":"1aa41178-c80c-4666-8fb3-b4b5cb65042f","word":"TV","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"abbreviation for television","tags":["feminine"],"word":"TV"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"abbreviation for television","tags":["feminine"],"word":"tevê"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"I saw an ad for that on TV.","bold_text_offsets":[[24,26]],"type":"example","id":"def438a2-855d-4118-9204-736a3e1cbf47"},{"text":"Believe me, the sun always shines on TV","ref":"1985, Paul Waaktaar-Savoy, “The Sun Always Shines on T.V.”, in Hunting High and Low, performed by a-ha:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[37,39]],"id":"c24c4003-7992-4b48-8c47-bf354e7131ae"},{"text":"USB-C isn’t just how many PC laptops are charged; it’s also how the Chromecast With Google TV draws power. It’s also the only USB port in any modern MacBook, and it’s used for charging and data transfer in many Samsung Galaxy phones (dating back to 2016’s infamous Galaxy Note 7).","ref":"2023 September 15, Henry T. Casey, “What is USB-C? Here’s everything you need to know”, in CNN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[91,93]],"id":"22401544-12fe-45f1-ac56-97ffbae3ba7c"}],"categories":["English abbreviations","English colloquialisms","English countable nouns","English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples","English uncountable nouns"],"links":[["television","television#English"]],"raw_glosses":["(colloquial, countable, uncountable) Abbreviation of television."],"glosses":["Abbreviation of television."],"tags":["abbreviation","alt-of","colloquial","countable","uncountable"],"alt_of":[{"word":"television"}],"id":"907d36a7-af94-4a6b-ab78-d7c7a2698177"},{"examples":[{"text":"1970-1975, Lou Sullivan, personal diary, quoted in 2019, Ellis Martin, Zach Ozma (editors), We Both Laughed In Pleasure\nShe spoke of her male side as her \"brother\" as do older, more conventional TVs.","id":"84ad9884-9a67-45f1-bde0-0f800d200d85"},{"text":"I am in isolation and am lonely and would like to correspond with TVs, TSs and queens.","ref":"1986 April 12, David Anderson, “Personal advertisement”, in Gay Community News, page 18:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[66,69]],"id":"a00e1278-58c5-4063-b4b3-2b2d43dc6189"},{"text":"TV's who dominate and TV's who are dominated! TV's who are hot, sexy and horny as hell!","ref":"1996, Forced Womanhood, number 20, page 32:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[0,2],[22,24],[46,48]],"id":"c7314842-6fb9-4ac6-9013-967c25f51040"}],"topics":["anatomy","medicine","sciences"],"wikidata":["Q1344255"],"senseid":["en:Q1344255"],"categories":["English countable nouns","English initialisms","English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned","en:Anatomy","en:Medicine"],"links":[["anatomy","anatomy"],["medicine","medicine"],["tricuspid valve","tricuspid valve#English:_Q1344255"]],"hypernyms":[{"word":"heart valve"},{"word":"valve"},{"word":"part"},{"word":"portion"}],"coordinate_terms":[{"word":"AoV"},{"word":"MV"},{"word":"PV"}],"raw_glosses":["(countable, anatomy, medicine) Initialism of tricuspid valve."],"glosses":["Initialism of tricuspid valve."],"tags":["abbreviation","alt-of","countable","initialism"],"alt_of":[{"word":"tricuspid valve"}],"id":"bbcca662-fd94-4b70-ade0-1d391b443cea"},{"topics":["medicine","physiology","sciences"],"wikidata":["Q3493813"],"senseid":["en:Q3493813"],"categories":["English initialisms","en:Medicine","en:Physiology"],"links":[["physiology","physiology"],["medicine","medicine"],["tidal volume","tidal volume#English:_Q3493813"]],"raw_glosses":["(physiology, medicine) Initialism of tidal volume."],"glosses":["Initialism of tidal volume."],"tags":["abbreviation","alt-of","countable","initialism","uncountable"],"alt_of":[{"word":"tidal volume"}],"id":"36f2bc96-00af-46a6-8352-1aa85f7d4b8f"},{"senseid":["en:tax value"],"categories":["English initialisms"],"links":[["tax value","tax value#English"]],"hyp